{
  "label": "concave",
  "explanation": "For f(x) = 1/(7/4 + e^x) on [-2,-1], the second derivative is f''(x) = e^x (e^x - 7/4) / (7/4 + e^x)^3. On this interval e^x ∈ [e^{-2}, e^{-1}] and e^{-1} < 7/4, so e^x - 7/4 < 0. With e^x > 0 and the denominator positive, f''(x) < 0 for all x in [-2,-1], hence f is concave on the interval."
}

